      "value": "@{5fcd676570b59138e6ef0271|full_name}: There may be a misunderstanding here. Contacts are synced since their position is synced. The docs (well, more specifically the info text on the component) mentions that it's not necessary to use a parameter defined on the VRCExpressionParameters object, which is true. What it means, specifically, is that a Receiver will drive a parameter defined only on an animator, and not on the VRCExpressionParameters, locally _and remotely_ (via the collision detection on the remote client).\n\nIt will however, as you mentioned, not sync the parameter itself over the network. This is intended behaviour and will not change.\n\nYou may however specify a parameter name on a Contact Receiver that matches one in VRCExpressionParameters, in which case you can make it sync that way. You do not need 2 parameters for that, 1 is enough for this to work. This will give you consistency at the cost of a synced parameter and a bit more latency - a tradeoff. As the info box also mentions, you should make the Contact Receiver \"Local Only\" in this case, as it would otherwise override the parameter synced value by also running the Receiver itself on the remote.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
