  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-01-10T22:07:43.962Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I am fully aware that this has been discussed in monthly meetings with creators and devs since avatar dynamics came out.  I figured I bring this up now as this has been a problem for nearly a year at this point. Avatar Contact parameters are not synced with the network as they were supposed to be. Due to how VRChat latency is handled Contacts rely on the network IK smoothening to determine if the contact has been touched instead of relying on the descriptor and/or animator. This is a problem when demonstating some avatars, as it would appear that I grabbed the object via contact interactions a few people they would see that I touched it, but no one else would notice that I touched it if they are have a higher latency than others in the instance.\n\n The current work around for this would be to manually sync the contacts by adding a parameter to the parameter list and using a parameter driver to sync it to the network. Users should not have to do this and it is honestly unacceptable that for months that some users have brought this up to the devs privately but hasn't been addressed at all.\n\nIt would be good to get the contacts to not rely on network IK to sync the contacts.",
